                        "entry_id": "4fdaa9d1-3c2b-3229-9cac-998e8b5def86",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The phrenic nerves; the nerves that control the diaphragm."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "addfb23b-f2d0-41a5-8b1e-d16ec2a8de12",
                                "sense_id": "c770f3c9-5163-3991-91e6-e4ef9ac44cfc",
                                "text": "One sees plainly, that while old rabbits, after removal of the influence of the phrenics, can still reach from ½ to 8/9 of the normal quantity of air used, in young animals the proportion stands so that they only respire from ¼ to 1/6 in one minute; and thus they satisfy their need of air so unsatisfactorily that they soon die."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7b0da8d-04f9-4867-9bab-bb97814d4de1",
                                "sense_id": "c770f3c9-5163-3991-91e6-e4ef9ac44cfc",
                                "text": "If the phrenics are both cut, the diaphragm is paralyzed; if a single one, that side only remains passive."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
